    improvTips: ['Bb major pentatonic drives the Third World reggae-pop fusion that made them Jamaica\'s second most internationally successful act after Marley','Gm (vi): "now that we found love, what are we gonna do with it?" — the vulnerability of love found — lives at the relative minor','Third World\'s jazz/rock influences (Stephen Cat Coore studied classical) reward the sophisticated musicianship beneath the reggae surface','The reggae fusion concept (reggae absorbing rock, jazz, soul) rewards understanding that Jamaican music was always an absorptive, not a purist, tradition'],
